# Root attributes. Architecture's file (plan.md 10.2, 2026-10-15).
# The Micro-Manager configurations that arrive with dino-autofocus must stay
# byte-exact against the microscope computer's originals: no end-of-line
# conversion on checkout or commit. Landed before the import commit.
microscope_agent/autofocus/configs/micromanager/*.cfg -text

# The person's files in the runtime (2026-10-19, the person, on the microscope
# computer). The live-view list is approved by the sha256 of its bytes, so a
# checkout that rewrites line endings gives the same approved file a different
# hash on each computer: on the microscope computer, with core.autocrlf true,
# the list read 1498acb5... on disk against the 82c7b36c... the person approved.
# No end-of-line conversion for any of them, so disk bytes equal committed bytes.
microscope_runtime/approvals/** -text
microscope_runtime/envelope/safety.json -text

# The console inbox (plan.md 7.1.1). A run log holds console_item.sha256 to the
# bytes of the item as the runner read them, and attachments are hashed too, so
# a checkout under core.autocrlf true must not rewrite line endings: disk bytes
# equal committed bytes, as for the approvals above. At any depth.
**/console_inbox/** -text
